1
00:00:50,625 --> 00:00:54,246
I love my school. I have so many good friends there now.

2
00:00:54,246 --> 00:00:56,581
I wouldn't miss a day even if I were really sick.

3
00:00:56,581 --> 00:01:02,537
Come and sit down for a minute, Michelle.

4
00:01:02,537 --> 00:01:05,515
I'd like to talk to you about something.

5
00:01:05,515 --> 00:01:08,493
Something important.

6
00:01:08,493 --> 00:01:10,493
What's wrong, Susan?

7
00:01:10,493 --> 00:01:11,471
Oh, there's nothing wrong, Michelle.

8
00:01:11,471 --> 00:01:14,449
But your daddy and I are talking about something

9
00:01:14,449 --> 00:01:16,449
that I'd like your opinion about.

10
00:01:16,449 --> 00:01:19,347
I know. I heard you talking about it

11
00:01:19,347 --> 00:01:22,558
the other night when I was trying on my new clothes.

12
00:01:22,558 --> 00:01:25,943
It's about moving to Los Angeles.

13
00:01:25,943 --> 00:01:29,339
You're right. How do you feel about it?

14
00:01:29,339 --> 00:01:35,295
Well, I really wouldn't want to move, but ...

15
00:01:35,295 --> 00:01:35,665
But?

16
00:01:35,665 --> 00:01:38,811
But if you and Daddy wanted to,

17
00:01:38,811 --> 00:01:43,251
I guess you know what's best for the family and for me.

18
00:01:43,251 --> 00:01:45,689
That's very considerate of you, Michelle.

19
00:01:45,689 --> 00:01:47,207
But what about your friends?

20
00:01:47,207 --> 00:01:48,571
I'd miss them a lot,

21
00:01:48,571 --> 00:01:52,372
but I know what it feels like to miss someone.

22
00:01:52,372 --> 00:01:54,163
Honey, we don't have to move

23
00:01:54,163 --> 00:01:56,412
if you're not going to be happy about it.

24
00:01:56,412 --> 00:01:57,772
Does Daddy want to move?

25
00:01:57,772 --> 00:02:02,290
I think so. He's going to tell us tonight about the job offer.

26
00:02:02,290 --> 00:02:09,292
Well, how was everybody's day today?

27
00:02:09,292 --> 00:02:12,697
Michelle was chosen to do Michelle

28
00:02:12,697 --> 00:02:15,468
the school poster for the play this year.

29
00:02:15,468 --> 00:02:16,441
Congratulations, Michelle! That's something!

30
00:02:16,441 --> 00:02:19,964
And how was your day, Susan?

31
00:02:19,964 --> 00:02:23,228
I see you're in a good mood.

32
00:02:23,228 --> 00:02:25,609
Why don't you tell us about your day.

33
00:02:25,609 --> 00:02:27,520
I met with Bill York.

34
00:02:27,520 --> 00:02:32,416
It's OK to talk about it, Harry.

35
00:02:32,416 --> 00:02:35,656
Michelle knows all about it. Michelle

36
00:02:35,656 --> 00:02:35,856
Really?

37
00:02:35,656 --> 00:02:36,654
Really, Harry.

38
00:02:36,654 --> 00:02:40,216
Michelle and I have all kinds of feelings Michelle

39
00:02:40,216 --> 00:02:43,650
about leaving New York, the family, and friends.

40
00:02:43,650 --> 00:02:46,766
But if you think you should take the job, we're behind you.

41
00:02:46,766 --> 00:02:49,744
What about Michelle's school?

42
00:02:49,744 --> 00:02:52,722
We'll move after the school term.

43
00:02:52,722 --> 00:02:54,722
What about her new friends?

44
00:02:54,722 --> 00:02:58,678
I'll make new friends wherever we are as long as we're together.

45
00:02:58,678 --> 00:03:01,656
We're a family, Harry.

46
00:03:01,656 --> 00:03:06,634
Whatever you think is right for you is right for us.

47
00:03:06,634 --> 00:03:11,589
I am so touched. The two of you are really something.

48
00:03:11,589 --> 00:03:13,967
We love you, Daddy.

49
00:03:13,967 --> 00:03:16,545
And I love you.

50
00:03:16,545 --> 00:03:21,203
OK. Now, tell us about your talk with Mr. York.

51
00:03:21,203 --> 00:03:22,283
Did you take the job?

52
00:03:22,283 --> 00:03:22,501
Nope.

53
00:03:22,501 --> 00:03:23,651
What?

54
00:03:23,651 --> 00:03:26,519
No? You didn't take it?

55
00:03:26,519 --> 00:03:29,457
No, I did not take the job.

56
00:03:29,457 --> 00:03:34,215
But, Daddy, I thought ...

57
00:03:34,215 --> 00:03:47,825
Harry, you didn't turn it down because of me ... Harry

58
00:03:47,825 --> 00:03:49,636
Or me?

59
00:03:49,636 --> 00:03:59,294
No, no. I turned it down because of me.

60
00:03:59,294 --> 00:03:59,717
How's that?

61
00:03:59,717 --> 00:04:26,238
Well, I began to think about you and about Michelle,

62
00:04:26,238 --> 00:04:47,217
and then I asked myself,

63
00:04:47,217 --> 00:05:00,774
do I really want to work for the biggest company in the country?

64
00:05:00,774 --> 00:05:11,126
And?

65
00:05:11,126 --> 00:05:15,664
And I don't.

66
00:05:15,664 --> 00:05:17,914
I went into business for myself

67
00:05:17,914 --> 00:05:20,286
because I like being my own boss.

68
00:05:20,286 --> 00:05:32,554
I run my own company. I'm a big fish in a little pond.

69
00:05:32,554 --> 00:05:45,443
I'm not really sure I want to be a little fish in a big pond.

70
00:05:45,443 --> 00:05:55,087
Oh, Daddy, does that mean we don't have to move?

71
00:05:55,087 --> 00:05:56,152
That's right, sweetheart.

72
00:05:56,152 --> 00:05:57,355
Are you sure?

73
00:05:57,355 --> 00:06:01,697
I couldn't be more sure, Susan.

74
00:06:01,697 --> 00:06:03,311
I'm glad if you are, Harry.

75
00:06:03,311 --> 00:06:10,371
And besides,

76
00:06:10,371 --> 00:06:13,609
how could I live in Los Angeles

77
00:06:13,609 --> 00:06:19,487
when all my favorite people live here?

78
00:06:19,487 --> 00:06:20,772
Your favorite people?

79
00:06:20,772 --> 00:06:21,679
Who's that?

80
00:06:21,679 --> 00:06:24,679
The Stewart family, of course.
